  "note": "variance-preserving Gaussian smoothing (noise_xi in stochastic.py): only the spatial correlation length changes, the local noise amplitude is fixed. Result: at fixed local amplitude, longer-range correlation makes the two interfering paths sample increasingly COMMON noise, suppressing the differential (relative) phase that destroys the fringes. The white-noise model (xi=0) is therefore the conservative worst case: it maximizes differential dephasing, so the paper's T_max = 11 K bound is a lower bound that holds for any environment with finite spatial correlation."
